# Admin Panel (`app/admin.py`)

Very large file (~3700 lines). Organised into clearly labelled sections with `# ===` comments.

## Permission Tiers
- Most routes: `@admin_required` — any subject admin or super admin
- User management: `@super_admin_required` — super admin only
- Health / File Browser: `@super_admin_required`
- Ingestion: `@admin_required` (filtered by user's admin subjects)

## Sections

### Subject Management (`/admin/subjects`) — super admin only
CRUD for the `Subject` model (historically only seeded by `init_db.py`).
- `GET /admin/subjects` — page (`admin_subjects.html`); table with per-subject question/topic/chapter counts.
- `GET /admin/subjects/<id>/usage` — JSON `{questions, topics, chapters, saved_filters, question_sets, permissions}` driving the delete-confirm modal. `saved_filters` is computed by parsing each `SavedFilter.filter_data` JSON for `subject == id` (helper `_saved_filter_subject_count`).
- `POST /admin/subjects/add` — `{id, name}`. ID is validated against `^[A-Z0-9]{1,10}$`, uppercased, must be unique (PK).
- `POST /admin/subjects/<id>/edit` — `{name}`. **Name only** — the ID is the PK, embedded in QIDs + the `SOURCE_PATH/<subject>/` layout, so it's immutable.
- `POST /admin/subjects/<id>/delete` — rejected (400) if any `Question` references it. Otherwise deletes `SavedQuestionSet`, stale `SavedFilter` rows (JSON match), `UserSubjectPermission`, then the `Subject` (topics/subtopics/chapters/subchapters cascade). Disk folder under `SOURCE_PATH` is left untouched.

### Topic Management (`/admin/topics`)
CRUD + reorder for Topics and Subtopics per subject.
- Topics/Subtopics have `sort_order` for drag-and-drop reorder
- Subtopics have `hidden` flag (hidden subtopics excluded from dashboard, but shown in admin with `include_hidden=1`)
- Same structure for Chapters/Subchapters at `/admin/chapters`

### Question Tagging (`POST /admin/questions/<id>/update`)
Updates question metadata fields: `major_topic_id`, `major_subtopic_id`, `minor_topics` (M2M), `subtopics` (M2M), `chapter_id`, `subchapter_id`, `level`, `q_type`, `section`, `description`, `correct_percentage`, `answer`, `comment`.  
Validation: `major_subtopic_id` must belong to `major_topic_id` when both are set.

### Question Management (`/admin/questions`)
- List with full filter support (same params as dashboard)
- `GET /admin/questions/api/list` accepts these mutually exclusive filters (first match wins):
  - `qids=Q1,Q2,...` — exact QID list (used by DB-Health anomaly view, preserves supplied order when sort is `selection_order`/`created_at`)
  - `selected_ids=1,2,3` — internal int IDs (used by "Show dashboard selections")
  - `qid_search=...` — LIKE substring/wildcard pattern
  - plus two **non-exclusive** filters: `verified` (`1`/`0`) and `check_status` (`issues`/`ok`/`unchecked` — asset-check rollup via correlated EXISTS). Each returned item also carries `verified` and `check_summary` (the rollup) for the **Status** + **Verified** list columns.
- Page reads `?qids=…` (or `?qids_token=…` → localStorage fallback) from URL on load and shows a dismissible banner; user typing in search or toggling dashboard-selections drops the pinned QID list.
- `POST /admin/questions/create` — create a question manually (without ingestor)
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/rename` — change QID (renames files on disk too, via `_build_asset_file_path`)
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/upload` — upload new asset file (IMG/DOC/MD; form field `version` (legacy `language` accepted); rejects a second MD for the same QUE/ANS/SOL × version (EN/CH/BI/ENO/CHO) slot and enforces `MD_MAX_SIZE_BYTES`)
- `DELETE /admin/questions/<id>/assets/<asset_id>` — delete asset (removes file from disk; invalidates MD render cache)
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/reorder` — update part_number ordering

### Markdown asset editor (MD only)
- `GET  /admin/questions/<id>/assets/<asset_id>/md/content` — JSON: raw text + `mtime_ns`
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/<asset_id>/md/save` — body `{content, expected_mtime_ns?, force?}`; 409 on optimistic conflict
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/md/create` — body `{version, asset_type, content}` (legacy `language` accepted); rejects 409 if MD exists in slot
- `GET  /admin/questions/<id>/assets/<asset_id>/md/edit` — fullscreen editor page (`templates/admin_md_editor.html`)
- `GET  /admin/questions/<id>/assets/md/new?version=&asset_type=` — fullscreen editor in create mode (legacy `language=` accepted)

Editor frontend lives in `templates/partials/md_editor.html` (EasyMDE + marked + KaTeX). The Edit Question modal in `admin_questions.html` includes both an **inline modal** editor (`#mdEditorModal`) and a link to the fullscreen variant per MD asset card.

### Batch Operations
`POST /admin/questions/batch-update` — selectively update multiple questions:
- Checkbox flags: `update_level`, `update_q_type`, `update_section`, `update_topics`, `update_correct_pct`
- `POST /admin/questions/delete` — delete multiple questions + cascade assets + delete files from disk
- `POST /admin/questions/batch_delete_assets` — delete a **filtered subset of assets** for the selected questions. Form params: `question_ids` (repeated), `formats` (repeated; IMG/MD/DOC), `versions` (repeated; EN/CH/BI/ENO/CHO; legacy `langs` accepted), `atypes` (repeated; QUE/ANS/SOL), `delete_files` (`true`/`false`, default `true`). Each axis must be non-empty (AND of three `IN(...)` clauses). Scope is intersected with the caller's admin subjects. Mirrors `delete_question_asset`'s DOC-thumbnail lifecycle hooks (`on_doc_asset_deleted` / `on_img_asset_deleted`) so cached PNGs stay consistent.
- `GET /admin/questions/batch-generate-images` — **SSE stream** that renders DOC/MD source assets into IMG PNGs in bulk. Query params: `question_ids` (csv), `types` (QUE/ANS/SOL), `versions` (EN/CH/BI/ENO/CHO; legacy `langs` accepted), `sources` (DOC/MD), `stitch` (1/0), `overwrite` (1/0), `width`, `transparent`. UI lives in the **Generate IMG** bulk button on `templates/admin_questions.html`. Backed by `app/batch_image_gen.py` (`render_doc_to_pages`, `render_md_to_pages`, `stitch_vertically`, `replace_img_assets`). Word COM serialised through the same global lock as DOC thumbnails / docx generation.
- `GET /admin/questions/batch-mcq-ans` — **SSE stream** that assigns MCQ answer images. For each selected question, reads `question.answer` (must be `A`/`B`/`C`/`D`) and `q_type` (must be `MC`), then copies the matching PNG from `resources/mcq_answer_img/{A|B|C|D}.png` into the canonical ANS slot on disk and upserts the `QuestionAsset` row. Query params: `question_ids` (csv), `versions` (csv, default `EN`; legacy `langs` accepted), `overwrite` (1/0, default `0`). Subject-admin permission. UI: **Set MCQ ANS** bulk button on `admin_questions.html`.

### AI Tools (LLM proofreading / Markdown generation)
- `GET /admin/questions/ai/check` and `GET /admin/questions/ai/generate-md` — **SSE streams** that call a configured LLM endpoint per question slot, with a real server-side Stop (`POST /admin/questions/ai/cancel` + `job_id`). `GET /admin/questions/ai/endpoints` lists enabled endpoints for the modal. `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/ai/generate-md` is the **synchronous** per-slot variant behind the edit-modal "Generate with AI" button, and `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/check-state` manually sets/clears a slot's proofread status (editable status bar). Subject-admin scoped; gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED` (the `window.OQB_AI_TOOLS_ENABLED` global in `base.html` exposes the per-slot UI to admins on both the admin page AND the dashboard). UI: **AI Tools** bulk button + `aiToolsModal` on `admin_questions.html`; per-slot button + editable check bar in `edit_question_modal_js.html`. Check results land on `QuestionAsset.check_state/check_result/checked_at`. See [ai-tools.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/ai-tools.mdc).
- **Auto Question Tagging** — `POST /admin/questions/<id>/ai/suggest-tags` (synchronous, **no write**: returns LLM suggestions for the edit modal to populate + highlight; user clicks Save Tags to commit) and `GET /admin/questions/ai/auto-tag` (**SSE** batch tagging, writes per question, reuses `/ai/cancel`). The model is sent QUE/SOL images (IMG → MD text → DOC-thumbnail fallback) + the subject's allowed tag values; returned names map back to Topic/Subtopic/Chapter/Subchapter IDs. Subject-admin scoped; gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED`. UI: **Auto Tag** button + `#autoTagModal` in the edit modal, **Auto tag** op in `aiToolsModal` for batch. See [ai-tools.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/ai-tools.mdc).
- **Verification + batch check-state** — `POST /admin/questions/<id>/verify` (`{verified}`; response carries `unchecked_assets` for the modal soft-warn), `POST /admin/questions/batch-set-verified` (`{question_ids[], verified}`), `POST /admin/questions/batch-set-check-state` (`{question_ids[], versions[], atypes[], state, note?, severity?, overwrite?}` — applies the per-slot proofread write across the selection). UI: **Set Check State** + **Set Verified** batch buttons on `admin_questions.html`; Verified toggle in the edit modal Details tab; **Status** + **Verified** filter dropdowns in the toolbar.
- **LLM Endpoints** (`/admin/llm-endpoints`, super-admin) — CRUD for `LLMConfig` rows: `llm_endpoints_page`, `llm_endpoints_data` (keys masked), `llm_endpoints_save` (encrypts a newly entered key; blank keeps existing; `clear_key` removes it), `llm_endpoints_<id>_delete`, `llm_endpoints_<id>_duplicate` (clones all fields except API key with auto-generated unique name), `llm_endpoints_<id>_test` (connectivity ping), `llm_endpoints_<id>_chat` (raw chat — passes `turns` straight to `llm_client.chat_messages` with no system prompt or context). UI `templates/admin_llm_endpoints.html`, linked from System Settings + Admin navbar.

The `Delete Selected` button on `admin_questions.html` opens a single two-tab modal — **Whole questions** (POSTs to `delete_questions`) and **Specific assets** (POSTs to `batch_delete_assets`). The shared confirm gate uses an "I understand" checkbox at ≤ 10 selected questions and requires typing `DELETE` above that threshold (`BULK_DELETE_TYPED_THRESHOLD = 10`). Switching tabs invalidates the confirm to force re-confirmation. The assets tab starts with **all checkboxes deselected** so nothing gets removed by accident.
- `POST /admin/questions/<qid>/assets/<aid>/rerender-thumb` — force a re-render of a single DOC asset thumbnail. Subject-admin only. Drives the per-preview "Re-render" button in dashboard cards / preview modal / inline preview helper. See [docx-source-format.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/docx-source-format.mdc) for the frontend flow.

### System Settings (`/admin/settings`) — super admin only
DB-backed runtime tunables that override `.env` / `Config` defaults without a restart. See [system-settings.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/system-settings.mdc) for the full reference.
- `GET  /admin/settings` — page (`templates/admin_settings.html`).
- `GET  /admin/settings/data` — `{groups, registry}` JSON for the UI.
- `POST /admin/settings/save` — body `{key: value, ...}`; per-key validation; partial saves succeed.
- `POST /admin/settings/reset/<key>` — drop DB override, restore bootstrap default.

The registry covers Dashboard / Markdown / Word COM / Thumbnails / Batch IMG / AI Tools groups. Secrets (DB creds, `SECRET_KEY`, paths, `PANDOC_PATH`, `DOC_THUMBNAIL_PATH`, `LLM_API_KEY`, `LLM_KEY_SECRET`) stay `.env`-only.

### User Management (`/admin/users`) — super admin only
- Add/edit/delete users
- `POST /admin/users/<id>/permissions` — set subject permissions (replaces all permissions for that user)
- Payload: `{subject_id: role}` dict where role is `'viewer'`, `'user'`, `'admin'`, or `''` to remove

### Export / Import (`/admin/export-import`)
All exports are CSV. Imports are idempotent (upsert logic).
- **Question Tags CSV**: `qid, subject, major_topic, major_subtopic, minor_topics, subtopics, chapter, subchapter, section, level, q_type, correct_percentage, description, answer, comment`
  - `GET /admin/export/question-tags` accepts either `subject_id` (full subject export) **or** `question_ids` (csv of DB IDs, exports only those questions filtered to the caller's admin subjects — used by the "Dashboard selections only" toggle on the Export page).
  - Output filename: `question_tags_{subject_id}.csv` or `question_tags_selected_{N}.csv`.
- **Topics CSV**: `subject_id, topic_name, subtopic_name, subtopic_hidden`. Row order = sort order.
- **Chapters CSV**: `subject_id, chapter_name, subchapter_name, subchapter_hidden`. Row order = sort order.

### Ingestion (`/admin/ingestion`)
- `GET /admin/ingestion/preview` — scan SOURCE_PATH, show directory tree + parseable file counts
- `GET /admin/ingestion/start?subject=MATC` — **SSE stream** that yields JSON progress events
  - Event types: `info`, `success`, `skip`, `error`, `progress`, `done`
  - `subject` param scans only `SOURCE_PATH/<subject>/` subfolder; omit to scan all
  - Uses `scan_directory_stream()` from `app/ingestor.py`

### PDF Batch Import (`/admin/pdf-import`)
Rasterise uploaded DSE question/solution PDFs, ask a vision LLM for a tight bounding box + printed question number per question per page, then crop + create `QUE`/`SOL` IMG assets. PP only; gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED` + a vision endpoint; subject-admin scoped. Backed by `app/pdf_import.py` (reuses `app/batch_image_gen.replace_img_assets`). Routes: `pdf_import_page`, `stage` (multipart upload+rasterise), `page/<token>/<kind>/<int:page>.png` (staged page PNG), `detect` (SSE), `redo-page` (POST), `plan` (POST, save edited plan), `commit` (SSE), `cancel` (POST), `discard` (POST). Two modes — Automatic (detect→commit) and Review (lightweight per-page box editor: delete/renumber/re-run, no manual drawing). Spanning questions → multi-part IMG. Tunable `PDF_IMPORT_RASTER_WIDTH`. See [pdf-import.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/pdf-import.mdc).

### Database Health (`/admin/health`) — super admin only
- `GET /admin/health/stats` — fast DB-only stats (counts, untagged, no-asset questions, duplicates, path mismatches)
- `GET /admin/health/untracked` — files on disk not in DB
- `GET /admin/health/sync?dry_run=1` — **SSE stream** to find/remove orphaned DB records
  - Grace period: questions created < 24h ago are skipped
- `GET /admin/health/doc-thumbnails/backfill?force=0|1` — **SSE stream** that walks every DOC asset and renders any missing PNG (or all PNGs when `force=1`).
- `POST /admin/health/doc-thumbnails/clear` — delete every cached PNG from `DOC_THUMBNAIL_PATH`. Lazy resolver re-creates them on demand.
- Anomaly modal (in `templates/admin_health.html`) tracks two parallel maps: `anomalyData` (display strings shown in the modal body) and `anomalyDataQids` (raw QIDs used by the "View in Dashboard" / "View in Question Management" footer buttons). For `duplicate_assets_list` and `path_mismatches_list`, the QID prefix is extracted from each formatted entry via `extractQidPrefix()`. The buttons pass QIDs via `?qids=…` URL param (or `?qids_token=…` with localStorage fallback when the joined list exceeds ~6 KB).

### File Browser (`/admin/files`) — super admin only
Browse, upload, download, rename, delete, copy, and duplicate files and directories within one of several **roots**.
- **Multiple roots.** `SOURCE_PATH` is the built-in, non-removable root. Super admins register extra roots in the **Manage roots** modal; they persist in `system_settings` under `FILE_BROWSER_EXTRA_ROOTS` (JSON list of abs paths; **not** in the settings REGISTRY — managed by dedicated routes). Every root must live on the **same drive as `SOURCE_PATH`** (`_browser_allowed_drive()` via `os.path.splitdrive`) so the browser can't reach `C:\` or unrelated shares.
- Every file op takes a `root` param (query/form/JSON `root`); `_request_browser_root()` → `_resolve_browser_root(id)` validates it is one of the allowed roots (id = normalised abs path) and returns the base for `_safe_join`. Invalid id → `400`. Missing → defaults to `SOURCE_PATH`.
- Root routes: `GET /admin/files/roots`, `POST /admin/files/roots/add` (`{path}`; validates exists+dir+on-drive+no-dup), `POST /admin/files/roots/remove` (`{id}`; can't remove Source; folder not deleted on disk).
- `POST /admin/files/copy` — copy one or more files/directories into a destination directory. Body: `{sources: [rel_paths], dest_dir: rel_path, root}`. Name conflicts resolved automatically with `_copy` / `_copy2` … suffixes (see `_unique_copy_name`). Prevents a folder being copied into itself. Uses `shutil.copy2` / `shutil.copytree`.
- Frontend clipboard: per-row **Copy** button + batch **Copy** in selection toolbar stash paths in an in-page `clipboard[]` array. **Paste here** toolbar button calls `POST /files/copy` with `dest_dir = currentPath`. Per-row **Duplicate** button (files only — folders use copy+paste) calls the same endpoint with the item's own parent as `dest_dir`.
- Folder single-delete requires typing `DELETE` (same pattern as batch delete). File single-delete is a simple confirm.

## Key Helper Function
`_build_asset_file_path(question, asset)` — reconstructs the canonical relative file path for an asset based on question fields. Used by rename and health path-mismatch check.
